//! The `image-orientation` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! specifies a layout-independent correction to the orientation of an image.
//!
//! Initial: from-image. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - flip: After rotating by the precededing angle, the image is flipped horizontally. Defaults to
//! 0deg if the angle is ommitted.
//! - from-image: Default initial value. The [EXIF](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EXIF) information
//! contained in the image is used to rotate the image appropriately.
//! - none: Does not apply any additional image rotation; the image is oriented as encoded or as
//! other CSS property values dictate.
//!
//! Grammar: from-image | none | [ <angle> || flip ]
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images-3/#propdef-image-orientation
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/image-orientation
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

